# The list of vir commands.
# This file is embedded into the `vir` binary at compile time.
#
# Syntax:
# Blank lines and `#` lines are ignored; trailing whitespace is trimmed.
# Lines ending in a colon specify a command group.
# The remaining lines are commands, together with their help messages.
# Commands are placed under the command group they belong to
#
# A "development command" is any command that is not listed here.
# They are those intended for Virdant developers rather than
# end users writing hardware: a convenience, test harness, or experimental tool.
# They are not listed in the --help.

Basic:
new         Create a new Virdant project
check       Check a Virdant project for problems
run         Run your design in the Virdant simulator

Tools:
doc         Create documentation for your project
format      Format your Virdant source files
lsp         Virdant Language Server

Flows:
build       Compile your design to Verilog
synth       Synthesize your design
pnr         Place-and-route your design
bitstream   Generate a bitstream for your FPGA
upload      Upload your design to your FPGA

About:
version     Print version information

Learning:
tutor       Generate a workspace for the Virdant tutorial
